          "body": "## Description\n\nCloses #7090\n\nWhen an asynchronous request lifecycle hook (`onRequest`, `preParsing`, `preValidation`, `preHandler`) calls `reply.send()`, the hook chain is intended to halt as documented in [Hooks.md](docs/Reference/Hooks.md#respond-to-a-request-from-a-hook):\n> \"Replying from a hook implies that the hook chain is stopped and the rest of the hooks and handlers are not executed.\"\n\nHowever, `reply.sent` previously evaluated solely as:\n```js\n(this[kReplyHijacked] || this.raw.writableEnded) === true\n```\nWhen two or more asynchronous `onSend` hooks are registered, the `onSend` execution chain is still in-flight on the microtask queue when the replying hook function promise resolves. Consequently, the hook runner callback (`preHandlerCallback`, `preValidationCallback`, etc.) observed `reply.sent === false` and proceeded to execute subsequent hooks and the route handler in parallel, allowing the handler to overwrite response status codes or throw `ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT`.\n\nThis PR introduces an internal `kReplySent` symbol to record when `reply.send()` has been invoked or reached the fallback error serialization stage:\n1. `this[kReplySent] = true` is set once `send()` is invoked with a payload or when `fallbackErrorHandler` begins emitting the response.\n2. `reply.sent` getter now evaluates `(this[kReplyHijacked] || this[kReplySent] || this.raw.writableEnded) === true`.\n3. If writing headers throws in `safeWriteHead` or execution transitions into `onErrorHook`, `this[kReplySent]` is reset to `false` to allow error handlers to proceed normally.\n4. Parameterized unit tests are added in `test/hooks-async.test.js` covering `onRequest`, `preParsing`, `preValidation`, and `preHandler` with multiple asynchronous `onSend` hooks.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] run `npm run test` and `npm run benchmark`\n- [x] tests and/or benchmarks are included\n- [x] documentation is changed or added\n- [x] commit message and PR title follows [commit guidelines](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#commit-guidelines)\n",
